1
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:06,620
Long ago, an already extraordinary
man wished for further power.

2
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:11,660
This man could soar like
a bird, swim like a fish,

3
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:16,000
breathe like a tree, and
move like a winding stream.

4
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:21,800
But sunlight spelled his doom,
so he created a stone mask.

5
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:26,977
One day, he would face
the sun without fear.

6
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:31,100
And then, the world would be his.

7
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:40,340
Vertigo, please tell me
cars fell into the lava.

8
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:48,420
I'm still alive. All right.

9
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:53,060
Must create armor.

10
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:56,460
Something like a clam.

11
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:59,580
Or a crab, a bony shell.

12
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:04,480
Yes, make me impervious!

13
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:13,360
It's not enough!

14
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:16,200
You dummy, that's lava!

15
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:18,580
It's a thousand degrees in there!

16
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,480
Now burn to a crisp, you cocky bastard!

17
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:34,210
Ouch!

18
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:38,310
Yes!

19
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:39,420
That did it!

20
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:41,710
Finally!

21
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:43,800
Kars was the last of them!

22
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:45,820
The Pillar Men are defeated!

23
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:01,940
The shock of his demise
triggered an eruption!

24
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:06,080
Let's get to safety before we
celebrate further! Good call!

25
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:07,713
Hang on tight, alright?

26
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:52,940
Music to my ears.

27
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:56,177
You perform that aria perfectly.

28
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:59,260
I've so longed to hear you sing it, Jojo!

29
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:04,100
Kars, you're alive!

30
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:07,380
A bit of his shell!

31
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:15,180
Inorganic, but of course!

32
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:21,341
Kars first covered himself in a
substance, not unlike a crab shell.

33
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:24,600
However, it was still organic.

34
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:26,500
It wasn't up to the task.

35
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:30,372
Faced with the heat of the
lava, it burned away instantly.

36
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:35,760
Luckily for Kars, he had the idea
to create a second layer of armor,

37
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:41,300
made of an unlikely
substance, mere air bubbles.

38
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:47,028
The bubbles maintained a pocket of air
between Kars' body and the lethal heat.

39
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:50,037
As the outer layer burned
away with each passing second,

40
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:53,057
But more bubbles worked their
way outward to replace them,

41
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,140
maintaining a perfect equilibrium.

42
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:58,592
Kars had the moments he needed to escape.

43
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:03,180
The Earth gave birth to life.

44
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,380
But now,

45
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:10,420
horror of horrors, Kars, a creature of the
Earth, has conquered the planet itself!

46
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:14,440
Eons ago,

47
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:19,340
long before man first thought to
chronicle his deeds, A group of creatures,

48
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:23,140
like us but not, evolved
alongside humanity.

49
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:25,657
The sun was lethal to them,

50
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:27,897
so they lived out their
lives under the cool

51
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:31,820
glow of the moon and in
their subterranean cities.

52
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:35,840
Even without the sun's sustaining rays,

53
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:41,240
they endured far longer than their human
rivals by feeding on other living things.

54
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:46,360
To humans that knew of their existence,
they were revered as gods or demons.

55
00:04:47,780 --> 00:04:51,368
Their numbers were small, as
few died and children were rare.

56
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:54,580
In all things, they
maintained a vital balance.

57
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:58,420
They knew no strife and lived
in peace with one another.

58
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:05,560
But then, a man of great pride
and ambition was born among them.

59
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:13,100
Strength is hidden within this body,
talents we cannot but dream of.

60
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:16,700
I shall be the one to unlock them.

61
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:20,660
To that end, he created a stone mask.

62
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:27,660
The mask granted him unheralded power,
but at a terrible, ravenous cost.

63
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:32,220
To survive, he had to consume
life at a dizzying rate.

64
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:36,813
If left unchecked, he would eventually
devour every living thing on Earth.

65
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:42,220
His brethren began to fear the mask, as
well as the gifted soul who created it.

66
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,637
His very existence is a threat!

67
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:49,040
There is no place for one
such as him in this world.

68
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:51,380
We have to wipe out his evil.

69
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,080
Look at you fools.

70
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:56,147
Don't you want to have
dominion over the sun?

71
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:59,200
To stand in ascendance over all life?

72
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:03,120
To purge your fears and
reign forever as gods?

73
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,600
If not, then die.

74
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:20,660
The Iconoclast brazenly
slaughtered his brethren,

75
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:24,084
even killing the parents
who had given him life.

76
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:28,137
He and his sole ally
took the two surviving

77
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:30,900
infants and left the scene of the carnage.

78
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:33,500
They set off in search of ultimate power,

79
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:36,408
a journey of continents
and centuries alike.

80
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:41,820
And now, 10,000 years later, that
power was in his hands at last.

81
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:48,417
He's a god this tyrant has become a deity

82
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:52,457
and against such a foe
there is nothing that

83
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:54,877
we can do we must submit

84
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:55,917
or perish

85
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:02,537
hear that

86
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:05,740
i think jojo is trying
to tell me something

87
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:13,060
Hamon overdrive!

88
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:15,460
What? Hamon?

89
00:07:17,740 --> 00:07:19,800
Did you say Hamon overdrive?

90
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:23,440
Jojo!

91
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:29,360
No, how?

92
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:32,320
My leg, it's melting away!

93
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,200
This is impossible!

94
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:35,870
Melting?

95
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:37,280
You don't mean to say!

96
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:38,380
It can't be!

97
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:41,460
Denial will get you nowhere, my friend.

98
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:42,940
Hamon did that!

99
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,920
I conquered the sun itself.

100
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:49,997
What makes you think that something
like Hamon was somehow beyond my reach?

101
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,477
I just...

102
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:53,501
Not only is Hamon at my disposal,

103
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,294
but it seems that mine is
hundreds of times more potent.

104
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:58,350
My god!

105
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:00,441
That's much stronger than Jojo's!

106
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:03,897
It's as though he brushed
his knee against the sun!

107
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:08,980
His flesh is liquefying and
vaporizing before his very eyes.

108
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:13,420
I wonder, how do you like the
taste of your own medicine?

109
00:08:16,060 --> 00:08:17,980
Hmm, a very articulate reply.

110
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:23,300
I suppose it's time to put
you out of your misery.

111
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:24,810
Jojo!

112
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:28,120
This is it.

113
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:30,280
I'm going to die here.

114
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:32,480
This is the end.

115
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:35,851
Jojo accepted his impending demise calmly.

116
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:40,660
He felt no fear, no pain,
no regret at his plight.

117
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:43,360
I did all I could, he told himself.

118
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:47,640
As the epitome of evil
loomed over Jojo in triumph,

119
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:50,760
he watched his dying self
with perfect clarity.

120
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,040
Stroheim felt much the same.

121
00:08:54,540 --> 00:09:00,500
Unable to move, he knew what snake prey
feels like as it stares into Oblivion's maw.

122
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:07,160
The power in a breath.

123
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:13,840
To think I will annihilate a practitioner
of Hamon with his own discipline.

124
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:21,540
Surely you can appreciate
the irony in that.

125
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,860
Ha... more?

126
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:29,357
Stronger than mine has ever been.

127
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:34,440
Let me be the first to
welcome you into oblivion!

128
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:36,520
Wait, Harmon?

129
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:43,877
What the...

130
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:46,200
the red stone?

131
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,457
What the...

132
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:54,080
the red stone?

133
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,640
The Red Stone of Asia!

134
00:10:00,940 --> 00:10:04,400
But why did Jojo brandish it
at Kars in that final moment?

135
00:10:04,580 --> 00:10:06,060
Even he had no idea!

136
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:08,797
As if by instinct,

137
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:13,174
he lunged the stone towards the
approaching Hamon to which it gravitated.

138
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:14,950
Saga!

139
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:19,040
Now, in a moment devoid of hope,

140
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:22,617
Jojo's body did the one thing
that could save his life!

141
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:27,560
Having survived Karr's coup de Crazy,
his will to live sprang into action.

142
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:32,020
Yes, the red stone amplifies Hamon!

143
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:38,600
Fueled by the magnified blast of Hamon,

144
00:10:39,060 --> 00:10:41,577
the volcano's fury reaches
the breaking point.

145
00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:42,960
It erupts!

146
00:10:50,580 --> 00:10:51,410
What?

147
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:53,420
They've blasted into the sky!

148
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:02,800
The force is strong, like
nothing I've ever known!

149
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:12,080
Do you really think a little eruption
will be enough to conquer the likes of me?

150
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:15,840
I'll just fly my way to safety.

151
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:20,160
Enjoy the fruits of your folly, Jojo!

152
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:24,480
Who's laughing now, huh?

153
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:29,180
Let me guess.

154
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:33,720
You're gonna say, did you
plan this too, Jojo? Tell me.

155
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:35,640
How do you always know?

156
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:40,480
For a moment, Kars was distracted by
Jojo's arm and his cocky attitude.

157
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:42,520
That moment was all it took.

158
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:48,722
Scalding rocks he didn't see coming launched
him even higher into the stratosphere!

159
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:53,420
Did you plan this too, Jojo? Tell me!

160
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:55,260
Why are you even asking?

161
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:58,100
I set the trap and you
walked right into it!

162
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:01,180
All of this went down like clockwork!

163
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:08,999
I just got lucky, but thinking I
outsmarted him will drive cars nuts!

164
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:11,420
At that moment,

165
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:15,699
the rocks launched by the volcano's
eruption reached escape velocity.

166
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:17,660
Kars was the perfect being!

167
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:19,757
Nothing on Earth could kill him!

168
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:24,880
But, just then, he was blasted
into the vacuum of space!

169
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:26,950
No!

170
00:12:27,033 --> 00:12:27,863
Damn you!

171
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:37,780
It's over.

172
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:44,657
Granny, and Stroheim, old Speedwagon,

173
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:49,700
Smoky, and Lisa Lisa.

174
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,340
Everyone, goodbye.

175
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:58,110
No.

176
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,190
JoJo!

177
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:07,017
Von Stroheim made it back to
the others eight hours later,

178
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:09,780
whereupon he told them this sad news.

179
00:13:21,580 --> 00:13:23,320
No! No!

180
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,100
Don't panic!

181
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:27,656
Just find the Earth!

182
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:33,797
I'll use air to change my trajectory.

183
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:37,760
Once I'm back on solid ground,
I will tear that boy apart!

184
00:13:57,880 --> 00:13:58,710
No!

185
00:13:58,793 --> 00:13:59,640
It's not working!

186
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:01,580
I'm freezing!

187
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:05,397
The air is freezing around me.

188
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:08,017
The moment it comes out of the jets!

189
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:09,560
It turns to ice.

190
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:16,157
I can't change my path.

191
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:18,460
I can't move.

192
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:25,717
So ended Kars?

193
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:28,380
Last and greatest of the Pillar Men.

194
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:34,680
His body turned hard as rock, and he
floated through space for the rest of time,

195
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:36,360
never to return.

196
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:41,280
He wished for death, but there
was nothing out there to kill him.

197
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:46,540
The spark of thought within
him went dim, and then silent.

198
00:14:57,580 --> 00:15:01,717
We commend his soul unto the
heavenly father though his life

199
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:05,860
on earth has ended far too
soon he lives in grace with you

200
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:12,080
comfort those he leaves behind Oh
God and let them know your peace

201
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:30,920
Goodbye, Jojo I didn't know you for too
long couldn't have been more than six months

202
00:15:33,980 --> 00:15:37,820
don't matter even though
you're gone I'm your friend

203
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:40,450
forever

204
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:47,417
Come, Iran.

205
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:49,437
It won't do to catch cold.

206
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:50,960
Let's get you home.

207
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,160
Just a bit longer.

208
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,280
Guess who?

209
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:03,320
What gives, fellas?

210
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:07,780
I finally make it to New York, and
nobody was there to pick me up!

211
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:12,660
Then, I got word you were all at a
funeral, so I decided to crash it.

212
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:14,460
Hey, Lisa Lisa!

213
00:16:14,780 --> 00:16:16,857
Guess you healed up pretty well, huh?

214
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:18,780
Messina, good to see you, too.

215
00:16:19,260 --> 00:16:20,436
New hand works well.

216
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:22,937
Though I've been meaning
to ask Stroheim if he can

217
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:25,961
jazz it up with a few
gadgets or tools or whatnot.

218
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:29,261
I guess that's right out
with us fighting Germany.

219
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:30,790
Hey, now!

220
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:32,617
You leave these mourners alone!

221
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:33,759
This is a funeral!

222
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,077
Show some respect, you own...

223
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:36,797
Oh, so I'm oaf, am I?

224
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:40,280
You need a lesson in manners,
and I'm glad to apply!

225
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:42,160
All right, calm down.

226
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:43,518
Let's not be hasty.

227
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:46,940
I'm sure you didn't mean
nothing by it. No way.

228
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:50,097
I'm talking to you, big
guy! You'd better...

229
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:51,440
Back off, man!

230
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:54,457
I'm just trying to catch up
with my family and friends.

231
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:55,370
JoJo!

232
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:59,580
You're telling me JoJo's alive?! Huh?

233
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:00,880
Yeah, of course.

234
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:02,952
Wait, what's this about?

235
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,957
You're all staring as
though you've seen a ghost.

236
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:07,180
I know it's a funeral, and uh-huh.

237
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:10,050
What the?

238
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,677
What's my name doing on there?

239
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:12,878
I'm alive and well!

240
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:14,845
Wait, this funeral was for me?

241
00:17:15,580 --> 00:17:16,410
Jojo!

242
00:17:16,493 --> 00:17:18,394
You're still recovering, you big silly.

243
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:20,838
Don't run off in the rain like that.

244
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:26,260
Here, take this.

245
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:29,560
Hey, that girl is Suzy Q.

246
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:32,157
And that ring looks like a...

247
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:35,416
Are you telling me you don't
know that we got married?

248
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:37,340
You got married?

249
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:39,500
Isn't it crazy?

250
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:41,000
Just think about it.

251
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:42,720
I'm officially Mrs.

252
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:44,860
Joseph Joestar. Goodness.

253
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:49,180
It makes me blush.

254
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:51,800
Wait a second here.

255
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:56,815
Suzy Q, something about this doesn't
feel right and I want to know what.

256
00:17:57,160 --> 00:18:00,897
The rock I was on fell into
the ocean and me along with it.

257
00:18:00,980 --> 00:18:02,627
A fishing boat picked me up.

258
00:18:02,860 --> 00:18:04,240
So far, so good.

259
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:08,957
You nursed me back to health in Venice
for two weeks, and we tied the knot.

260
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:11,216
So why did they all think I was dead?

261
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:15,560
You never sent that telegram
like I asked, did you?

262
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:18,900
Uh, I don't really know.

263
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:20,920
To me, that sounds like no.

264
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:28,100
Uh, now, now, let's not
get all clicky fingers.

265
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:30,520
I never sent it!

266
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:31,860
I'm sorry, JoJo!

267
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:33,680
Ah! Suzy Q!

268
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:35,000
What the hell?

269
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,380
You had one job, woman! One job!

270
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:40,050
Ah!

271
00:18:40,133 --> 00:18:41,940
JoJo came back to us all!

272
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:43,750
Stop it!

273
00:18:43,833 --> 00:18:45,520
I said I was sorry! Sorry?

274
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,132
They thought I was dead!

275
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:50,270
JoJo.

276
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:53,080
Soon after, Lisa Lisa, a .k .a.

277
00:18:53,220 --> 00:18:56,577
Elizabeth Joestar, told JoJo
that she was his mother.

278
00:18:56,660 --> 00:18:58,760
they moved to America.

279
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:04,980
In 1948, she found love again and
married a Hollywood screenwriter.

280
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:11,380
Iran Joestar continued
her work as a teacher.

281
00:19:13,220 --> 00:19:16,200
In 1950, she died
peacefully at the age of 81,

282
00:19:16,580 --> 00:19:19,345
surrounded by family and
friends who loved her.

283
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:24,100
Robert E .O.

284
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:28,320
Speedwagon continued to pour his
energy into philanthropic research,

285
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:31,937
helping to further science and
medicine in countless ways.

286
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:36,240
He died in 1952 of a heart
attack at 89 years of age.

287
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:39,820
A lifelong bachelor, he
left no family behind.

288
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:45,781
Smokey Brown went on to work his way through
college, majoring in political science.

289
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:51,788
Later, he became the first black mayor
of a city in his home state of Georgia.

290
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:56,697
Major Rudolph von Stroheim
would never see Jojo

291
00:19:56,780 --> 00:20:00,817
again he died in 1943 at
the battle of Stalingrad.

292
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:03,857
A fearsome example of
the German science he'd

293
00:20:03,940 --> 00:20:07,020
always championed our
technology is the greatest.

294
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:20,580
And so the years flowed
by to a new generation.

295
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:24,020
And as for JoJo...

296
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:28,460
Oh, breaking the leg, huh?

297
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,640
Sorry about that.

298
00:20:29,980 --> 00:20:31,597
You should watch where you're going.

299
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:33,637
You wouldn't want a
broken bone at your age.

300
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:34,550
You're right.

301
00:20:34,633 --> 00:20:35,800
How careless of me.

302
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:39,200
I guess this is a case
of live and learn. Hmm?

303
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:40,820
Hey, wait a sec.

304
00:20:41,060 --> 00:20:44,320
You're Japanese, aren't
you? I am. Why do you ask?

305
00:20:44,420 --> 00:20:46,580
In that case, watch your damn bag!

306
00:20:58,100 --> 00:21:02,620
My only daughter has been married
to a Japanese man for over 20 years.

307
00:21:02,940 --> 00:21:07,058
Fell in love on the other side of
the world and never came home again.

308
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:09,965
Her son rarely gets to
see his own grandfather.

309
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:13,280
That's why I'll never
forgive the Japanese.

310
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:20,180
Then again, they make
some rather nifty gadgets.

311
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:22,117
Yeah, that's true, we're gonna
get yasura no Seiko o tsuka!

312
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:27,620
Dario ni ta omoi ga, Mariah no Cairo ko?

313
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:33,157
Like a burning stone,
hot-suk like a burning stone.

314
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:36,797
Ketsu Mega ni kizamareta yunan ni.

315
00:22:36,880 --> 00:22:41,180
Uki no ni kei wa koi no kizuna.

316
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:45,280
Niigiri shimete.

317
00:22:57,320 --> 00:22:59,960
All right, it's finally
time to haul it up.

318
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:01,120
Oh, man.

319
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:03,737
What do you think's inside it, you guys?

320
00:23:03,820 --> 00:23:05,960
A hundred-year-old chest like that?

321
00:23:06,140 --> 00:23:07,440
It could be anything.

322
00:23:08,020 --> 00:23:10,140
Come on, let's open that bad boy.
